<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25123" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭtĭnĕrārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		iter, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a journey</i> or <i>march</i>, <i>itinerary</i> (late
			Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sumptus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lampr. Commod. 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">motus,</span>”
				<i>the motion of travelling</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 21, 15, 2</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭtĭnĕrārĭum</span></b> ,
				i, n.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>An account of a journey</i>, <i>an
				itinerary</i>, <i><span class="en">Veg. Mil. 3, 6</span></i>.
			— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A signal for marching</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">itinerarium sonare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 24, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
